{
 "about": "Console leaves of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'): the three leaves on the bell of the console over the left column, traced on the Palace Museum copy (album_2.jpg, public domain) in its own pixels, left half; the right half mirrors it about x 2136, the console's centre. Each leaf is a raised border round a sunk (dark) face carrying a column of four small raised arrowheads (a chevron with a short stem) pointing up, clear of the border; the middle leaf has a bead above them; the side leaves lean in towards the middle one and the leaves run under the pedestal's cap at y 1440, where the drawing stops. Bands are raised straps of the given width along a Catmull-Rom centre line; Each leaf's face is ground; ground_at marks the side leaf's face between its arrows, which come close enough to the border to close it into pockets.",
